{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "h4-rollout-icons",
  "title": "Support Assistant: Memory and Staged Rollout",
  "description": "How the customer support assistant handles a turn, keeps long-term memory, and ships new variants.\n\n- **Chat Surfaces** (top left): the customer reaches the assistant through web and mobile chat.\n- **Assistant Turn**: *Guarded Generation* runs input safety screen → assistant runtime → reply model call → output safety screen. *Context Retrieval* has two groups: *Articles* (article search over the help-center corpus) and *State* (the customer profile and the live conversation store). *Integrations*: billing and account integrations fetch credentials per call from the managed secrets vault.\n- **Escalation** (top right): a screened-out reply or flagged input gets the safe fallback reply. Repeated triggers, or a customer asking for a human, hand off to a human support agent.\n- **Live Quality Monitoring** (right, under escalation): per-variant metrics come from the runtime. A regression pulls the challenger from the traffic split.\n- **Memory** (bottom left), the long-term memory lifecycle, in two subsections. *Facts*: ended transcripts go to fact extraction, then a contradiction check that either supersedes the old profile fact (recording the source) or adds a new one. *Raw History*: raw conversations past the retention window move to cold storage.\n- **Variant Rollout** (bottom right), three subsections. *Versioned Variant Config* (left): champion and challenger feed a sampled traffic split that configures the runtime; the displaced champion is kept for a one-step rollback. *Experiment* (top right): judges score completed conversations into a report, which is checked against the bar. *Approval* (bottom right): product owner review, then approve (the challenger becomes champion) or reject.\n\nWire colors: green = replies or promotion, red = block, pull or reject, blue = memory reads and writes, violet = variant config, teal = actions and metrics.",
  "mode": "diagram",
